element.definition:
Initial TB patient classification. The source register requires one:

New;
Relapse;
Treatment after failure;
Treatment after loss to follow-up;
Other previously treated;
Unknown previous TB treatment history;
Transferred in.

Monitoring time point represented in the source register.

Expected values:
month-0;
month-2-or-3;
month-5;
month-6.

Final TB treatment outcome.

Source categories are:
Cured;
Treatment completed;
Treatment failed;
Died;
Lost to follow-up;
Not evaluated;
Removed from TB treatment register.

HIV testing outcome for a patient whose status was previously unknown.

Source values are:
Positive;
Negative;
Not Tested.

HIV status at the end of TB treatment.
Source values are:
Positive;
Negative;
Unknown.

